<div>
    <div class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <p>But rapid adoption is only the surface. Innovation is compoundin=
g; forces aren=E2=80=99t simply additive, but multiplicative. Think of it a=
s a flywheel: Better technology enables more applications. More application=
s generate more data. More data attracts more investment. More investment b=
uilds better infrastructure. Better infrastructure reduces costs. Lower cos=
ts enable more experimentation. Each improvement simultaneously accelerates=
 all the others.</p>
<p>It=E2=80=99s why AI startups scale from US$1 million to US$30 million in=
 revenue five times faster than SaaS companies did.<sup><a href=3D"https://=
www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.ht=
ml#endnote-3" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 3">3</a></sup> It=E2=
=80=99s why the knowledge half-life in AI has shrunk to months from years.<=
sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-ma=
nagement/tech-trends.html#endnote-4" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference numbe=
r 4">4</a></sup> And it=E2=80=99s why one chief information officer (CIO) t=
old me, =E2=80=9CThe time it takes us to study a new technology now exceeds=
 that technology=E2=80=99s relevance window.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p><b>Every organization we studied is discovering the same truth: What got=
 them here won=E2=80=99t get them there.</b></p>
<p>The infrastructure built for cloud-first strategies can=E2=80=99t handle=
 AI economics. Processes designed for human workers don=E2=80=99t work for =
agents. Security models built for perimeter defense don=E2=80=99t protect a=
gainst threats operating at machine speed. IT operating models built for se=
rvice delivery don=E2=80=99t drive business transformation.</p>
<p><b>This isn=E2=80=99t only about enhancement. It=E2=80=99s about rebuild=
ing.</b></p>
<p>For 17 years, Tech Trends has explored emerging technologies poised to r=
eshape business in the next 18 to 24 months. Our research is based on trend=
 sensing from conversations with Deloitte subject matter experts and extern=
al technology leaders, as well as Deloitte=E2=80=99s proprietary research o=
n emerging technologies. This year, the data reveals five interconnected fo=
rces.</p>

    </div>
</div>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text cmp-di-text pt-1 pb-1 pl-mob-2 pr-mob-2 aem-GridColumn--=
phone--12 cmp-di-text--line-height-large cmp-di-text-bullets">

   =20

<div class=3D"hide-no-results-error-msg">
    <img src=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/insights/icons/svg/ico=
n-alert.svg"> =20
</div>
<div>
    <div id=3D"Robots-and-physical" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h2>AI goes physical: Navigating the convergence of AI and robotics=
&nbsp;&nbsp;</h2>
<p>Amazon deployed its millionth robot, and its DeepFleet AI coordinates th=
e entire robot fleet, improving travel efficiency within warehouses by 10%.=
<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-m=
anagement/tech-trends.html#endnote-5" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference numb=
er 5">5</a></sup> BMW=E2=80=99s factories have cars driving themselves thro=
ugh kilometer-long production routes.<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.c=
om/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-6" =
aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 6">6</a></sup> Intelligence isn=E2=
=80=99t confined to screens anymore; it=E2=80=99s embodied, autonomous, and=
 solving real problems in the physical world.</p>

    </div>
</div>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text cmp-di-text pt-1 pb-1 pl-mob-2 pr-mob-2 aem-GridColumn--=
phone--12 cmp-di-text--line-height-large cmp-di-text-bullets">

   =20

<div class=3D"hide-no-results-error-msg">
    <img src=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/insights/icons/svg/ico=
n-alert.svg"> =20
</div>
<div>
    <div id=3D"agentic-reality" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h2>The agentic reality check: Preparing for a silicon-based workfo=
rce</h2>
<p>Only 11% of organizations have agents in production, despite 38% pilotin=
g them. The gap between pilot to production tells you everything. Forty-two=
 percent are still developing their strategy, while 35% have no strategy at=
 all.<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technol=
ogy-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-7" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference=
 number 7">7</a></sup> Gartner predicts that 40% of agentic projects will f=
ail by 2027<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/t=
echnology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-8" aria-label=3D"Endnotes ref=
erence number 8">8</a></sup>=E2=80=94not because the technology doesn=E2=80=
=99t work, but because organizations are automating broken processes instea=
d of redesigning operations. HPE=E2=80=99s chief financial officer captured=
 what works: =E2=80=9CWe wanted to select an end-to-end process where we co=
uld truly transform, not just solve for a single pain point.=E2=80=9D<sup><=
a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-managem=
ent/tech-trends.html#endnote-9" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 9">=
9</a></sup> Redesign, don=E2=80=99t automate. That=E2=80=99s the pattern se=
parating success from failure.</p>

    </div>
</div>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text cmp-di-text pt-1 pb-1 pl-mob-2 pr-mob-2 aem-GridColumn--=
phone--12 cmp-di-text--line-height-large cmp-di-text-bullets">

   =20

<div class=3D"hide-no-results-error-msg">
    <img src=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/insights/icons/svg/ico=
n-alert.svg"> =20
</div>
<div>
    <div id=3D"infrastructure-reckoning" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h2>The AI infrastructure reckoning: Optimizing compute strategy in=
 the age of inference economics</h2>
<p>Token costs have dropped 280-fold in two years;<sup><a href=3D"https://w=
ww.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.htm=
l#endnote-10" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 10">10</a></sup> yet =
some enterprises are seeing monthly bills in the tens of millions. Usage ex=
ploded faster than costs declined. Organizations are discovering their exis=
ting infrastructure strategies aren't designed to scale AI to production-sc=
ale deployment.&nbsp;They're shifting from cloud-first to strategic hybrid:=
 cloud for elasticity, on-premises for consistency, and edge for immediacy.=
</p>

    </div>
</div>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text cmp-di-text pt-1 pb-1 pl-mob-2 pr-mob-2 aem-GridColumn--=
phone--12 cmp-di-text--line-height-large cmp-di-text-bullets">

   =20

<div class=3D"hide-no-results-error-msg">
    <img src=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/insights/icons/svg/ico=
n-alert.svg"> =20
</div>
<div>
    <div id=3D"tech-organization" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h2>The great rebuild: Architecting an AI-native tech organization<=
/h2>
<p>AI is restructuring tech organizations, making them leaner, faster, and =
more strategic. Only 1% of IT leaders surveyed by Deloitte reported that no=
 major operating model changes were underway.<sup><a href=3D"https://www.de=
loitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.html#end=
note-11" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 11">11</a></sup>&nbsp;Lead=
ers are shifting from incremental IT management to orchestrating human-agen=
t teams, with CIOs becoming AI evangelists. Success requires bold reimagina=
tion: modular architectures, embedded governance, and perpetual evolution a=
s core capabilities.</p>

    </div>
</div>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text cmp-di-text pt-1 pb-1 pl-mob-2 pr-mob-2 aem-GridColumn--=
phone--12 cmp-di-text--line-height-large cmp-di-text-bullets">

   =20

<div class=3D"hide-no-results-error-msg">
    <img src=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/insights/icons/svg/ico=
n-alert.svg"> =20
</div>
<div>
    <div id=3D"cybersecurity-dilemma" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h2>The AI dilemma: Securing and leveraging AI for cyber defense</h=
2>
<p>The technology meant to give businesses an advantage is becoming the tar=
get used against them. AT&amp;T=E2=80=99s chief information security office=
r <a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-mana=
gement/tech-trends/2025/att-ai-cybersecurity-practices.html">captured the c=
hallenge</a>: =E2=80=9CWhat we=E2=80=99re experiencing today is no differen=
t than what we=E2=80=99ve experienced in the past. The only difference with=
 AI is speed and impact.=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/u=
s/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-12" ari=
a-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 12">12</a></sup>&nbsp;Organizations mu=
st secure AI across four domains=E2=80=94data, models, applications, and in=
frastructure=E2=80=94but they also have the opportunity to use AI-powered d=
efenses to fight threats operating at machine speed.</p>
<p>Throughout this year=E2=80=99s report, you=E2=80=99ll meet technology le=
aders successfully navigating this sea change. They don=E2=80=99t have all =
the answers, but there are noticeable patterns as they light the way forwar=
d.</p>
<ul><li><b>They lead with problems, not technology. </b>Broadcom=E2=80=99s =
CIO: =E2=80=9CWithout focusing on a specific business problem and the value=
 you want to derive, it could be easy to invest in AI and receive no return=
.=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/te=
chnology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-13" aria-label=3D"Endnotes ref=
erence number 13">13</a></sup></li><li><b>Specifically, their biggest probl=
ems.</b> UiPath CEO: =E2=80=9CRather than getting stuck in a cycle of perpe=
tual proofs of concept, consider attacking your biggest problem and going f=
or a big outcome.=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/in=
sights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-14" aria-label=
=3D"Endnotes reference number 14">14</a></sup></li><li><b>They prioritize v=
elocity over perfection. </b>Western Digital=E2=80=99s CIO: =E2=80=9CWe=E2=
=80=99d rather fail fast on small pilots than miss the wave entirely.=E2=80=
=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technolog=
y-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-15" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference =
number 15">15</a></sup></li><li><b>They design <i>with</i> people, not just=
 <i>for </i>them.</b> Walmart involved store associates in building its sch=
eduling app, which includes shift swapping, schedule visibility, and employ=
ee control. The result: Scheduling time dropped from 90 minutes to 30 minut=
es, and people actually used the app.<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.c=
om/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-16"=
 aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 16">16</a></sup></li><li><b>They t=
reat change as continuous.</b> Coca-Cola=E2=80=99s CIO described their jour=
ney as moving from =E2=80=9CWhat can we do?=E2=80=9D to =E2=80=9CWhat shoul=
d we do?=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/to=
pics/technology-management/tech-trends.html#endnote-17" aria-label=3D"Endno=
tes reference number 17">17</a></sup>&nbsp;That shift=E2=80=94from capabili=
ty-first to need-first=E2=80=94is what separates productive experimentation=
 from pilot purgatory.</li></ul>
<p>I=E2=80=99ve tracked technology evolution long enough to recognize the p=
atterns. The internet changed everything. Mobile reshaped consumer behavior=
. Cloud computing was transformative.</p>
<p>But this moment is different.</p>
<p>It=E2=80=99s not just that AI is powerful. It=E2=80=99s that the <a href=
=3D"https://rmi.org/insight/harnessing-the-power-of-s-curves/">S-curves</a>=
 are compressing. The distance between emerging and mainstream is collapsin=
g.</p>
<p>Organizations built for sequential improvement can=E2=80=99t compete wit=
h those operating in continuous learning loops. The traditional playbook as=
sumed you had time to get it right. That assumption no longer holds.</p>
<p>The organizations that succeed will probably not be those with the most =
sophisticated technology. They=E2=80=99ll be those with the courage to rede=
sign rather than automate, the discipline to connect every investment to bu=
siness outcomes, and the velocity to execute before the window closes.</p>
<p>Innovation compounds. The gap between laggards and leaders grows exponen=
tially. How you respond determines which side of that gap you=E2=80=99re on=
.</p>
<p>But you don=E2=80=99t have to navigate this alone. We hope this year=E2=
=80=99s publication reminds you that everyone=E2=80=99s facing this rapid p=
ace of change, and together, we can shape what comes next.</p>
<p><b>&nbsp;</b></p>
